# PATCH: 003-restrict-clipboard
#
# Blocks clipboard and drag-to-copy access, with an optional compile-time
# allow-list that permits in-browser copy/paste between configured sites.
#
# CORE BLOCKS (always active - six entry points):
#
# 1. Clipboard::ReadHelper (dom/events/Clipboard.cpp)
#    Blocks Clipboard.read() and Clipboard.readText() for all sites.
#
# 2. Clipboard::Write (dom/events/Clipboard.cpp)
#    Blocks Clipboard.write() and writeText() for all sites.
#
# 3. Document::ExecCommand (dom/base/Document.cpp)
#    Blocks document.execCommand("cut/copy/paste") for all sites.
#
# 4. nsCopySupport::FireClipboardEvent (dom/base/nsCopySupport.cpp)
#    Blocks user copy/cut commands for non-allowlisted content before native
#    clipboard work. Allowlisted sites fall through to the internal clipboard
#    path.
#
# 5. nsBaseClipboard::SetData (widget/nsBaseClipboard.cpp)
#    Suppresses remaining OS clipboard writes and skips ClipboardCache updates,
#    preventing allowlisted internal data from leaking through the native cache.
#
# 6. nsBaseDragSession::InvokeDragSession (widget/nsBaseDragService.cpp)
#    Blocks drag-and-drop to prevent text exfiltration through browser chrome.
#
# INTERNAL CLIPBOARD (optional - activated by site-config.json):
#
#   Copy from an allowlisted site follows Firefox's native encoder into
#   ContentParent::RecvSetClipboard, which captures text/plain in parent-process
#   memory and records the OS clipboard sequence number. nsBaseClipboard then
#   suppresses the OS write. This avoids shadow-DOM duplication from manual
#   selection encoding.
#
#   Paste on an allowlisted site sets gDenServePasteFromInternal in
#   FireClipboardEvent. nsClipboardProxy fetches the parent-held value through
#   synchronous IPC. If an external application has changed the OS clipboard
#   sequence number, the internal value is cleared and Firefox falls through to
#   the normal OS clipboard path, allowing external data to flow in without
#   exposing DenBrowser-internal data outside the browser.
#
# BLOCKED-ACTION FEEDBACK:
#
#   DenBrowserClipboardChild/Parent are all-frame actors that forward only
#   trusted DenBrowserCopyBlocked events to the owning live browser or opener.
#   Events cover denied copy/cut commands, execCommand cut/copy, and Clipboard
#   API writes when the attempt has valid transient user activation.
#
#   nsClipboardProxy passes the child-computed activation state over PContent so
#   ContentParent can notify other user-activated direct clipboard writers
#   without querying an out-of-process window. about:logins copy buttons take a
#   dedicated earlier route: they dispatch the blocked action before password
#   authentication, success UI, secret-detail construction, or ClipboardHelper;
#   the existing privileged actor notifies the owning browser without sending
#   the login value to the parent.
#
#   Parent-chrome context-menu copy actions, including regular and canvas image
#   copying, notify directly before transferable, canvas, actor, or clipboard
#   work. Patch 004 owns the shared non-modal per-tab notification.
#
# RELATIONSHIP TO PREFS:
#
#   lockPref("dom.allow_cut_copy", false) and
#   lockPref("dom.event.clipboardevents.enabled", false) are defense in depth.
#   This patch remains the authoritative clipboard control and the prefs do not
#   disable the allowlisted internal clipboard.


